IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc1-support`

-- ccc1-s26-33-force.l4 -- Part I (General), sections 26 to 33: excessive force, preventing an offence, force on board an aircraft, arrest of the wrong person,
-- the duties of a person who arrests or executes a process or warrant, preventing a breach of the peace, and the suppression of riots.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- A justification or protection ("is justified", "is protected") is a defence: where its "if" or "Where" gate is not met the answer is JUST FALSE, read as "this section gives no justification (or protection) on
-- these facts" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)); a "who" description not met answers NOTHING. Answers of section 2 ("peace officer") are INPUTS, MAYBE BOOLEAN, carried through when NOTHING.
-- The duties of sections 29(1), 29(2) and 33(1) are encoded twice: as regulative rules (run with #TRACE) and as decision functions (asserted).
-- The core `Party` has no constructor for "a person who executes a process or warrant" or "a person who arrests", so section 29 declares its own actor type; section 33(1) uses the core's `a peace officer`.

§ `Section 26 -- Excessive force`

-- src:727 | Excessive force
-- src:728 | 26 Every one who is authorized by law to use force is criminally responsible for any excess thereof according to the nature and quality of the act that constitutes the excess.
@ref s 26 (src:727-728)
GIVEN `the person is authorized by law to use force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force used is in excess of what the law authorizes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26 the person is criminally responsible for the excess of force` MEANS
    IF `the person is authorized by law to use force` AND `the force used is in excess of what the law authorizes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who is authorized by law to use force is criminally responsible for any excess thereof"

§ `Sections 27 and 27.1 -- Use of force to prevent commission of offence; on board an aircraft`

-- src:729 | Use of force to prevent commission of offence
-- src:730 | 27 Every one is justified in using as much force as is reasonably necessary
-- src:731 | (a) to prevent the commission of an offence
-- src:732 | (i) for which, if it were committed, the person who committed it might be arrested without warrant, and
-- src:733 | (ii) that would be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to the person or property of anyone; or
-- src:734 | (b) to prevent anything being done that, on reasonable grounds, he believes would, if it were done, be an offence mentioned in paragraph (a).
@ref s 27 (src:729-734)
GIVEN `the force is used to prevent the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who committed the offence, if it were committed, might be arrested without warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence would be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to the person or property of anyone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force is used to prevent anything being done that, on reasonable grounds, the person believes would, if it were done, be an offence mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force is as much as is reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27 the person is justified in using the force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the force is as much as is reasonably necessary` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "justified in using as much force as is reasonably necessary"
        IF `the force is used to prevent the commission of an offence` AND `the person who committed the offence, if it were committed, might be arrested without warrant` AND `the offence would be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to the person or property of anyone` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the force is used to prevent anything being done that, on reasonable grounds, the person believes would, if it were done, be an offence mentioned in paragraph (a)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (a) and (b) name two purposes and the section does not say "only"

-- src:735 | Use of force on board an aircraft
-- src:736 | 27.1 (1) Every person on an aircraft in flight is justified in using as much force as is reasonably necessary to prevent the commission of an offence against this Act or another Act of Parliament that the person believes on reasonable grounds, if it were committed, would be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to the aircraft or to any person or property therein.
@ref s 27.1(1) (src:735-736)
GIVEN `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is on the aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is against this Act or another Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person believes on reasonable grounds that the offence, if it were committed, would be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to the aircraft or to any person or property therein` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force is as much as is reasonably necessary to prevent the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27.1(1) the person on the aircraft is justified in using the force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 7(8) does not say whether the aircraft is in flight at that instant
        IF (`the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the person is on the aircraft`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person on an aircraft in flight"
        IF NOT (`the offence is against this Act or another Act of Parliament` AND `the person believes on reasonable grounds that the offence, if it were committed, would be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to the aircraft or to any person or property therein`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence against this Act or another Act of Parliament that the person believes on reasonable grounds, if it were committed, would be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to the aircraft or to any person or property therein"
        IF NOT `the force is as much as is reasonably necessary to prevent the commission of the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "justified in using as much force as is reasonably necessary"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:737 | Application of this section
-- src:738 | (2) This section applies in respect of any aircraft in flight in Canadian airspace and in respect of any aircraft registered in Canada in accordance with the regulations made under the Aeronautics Act in flight outside Canadian airspace.
@ref s 27.1(2) (src:737-738)
GIVEN `the aircraft is in flight in Canadian airspace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aircraft is registered in Canada in accordance with the regulations made under the Aeronautics Act and is in flight outside Canadian airspace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27.1(2) section 27.1 applies in respect of the aircraft` MEANS
    IF `the aircraft is in flight in Canadian airspace` OR `the aircraft is registered in Canada in accordance with the regulations made under the Aeronautics Act and is in flight outside Canadian airspace`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any aircraft in flight in Canadian airspace and in respect of any aircraft registered in Canada in accordance with the regulations made under the Aeronautics Act in flight outside Canadian airspace"

§ `Section 28 -- Arrest of wrong person`

-- src:739 | Arrest of wrong person
-- src:740 | 28 (1) Where a person who is authorized to execute a warrant to arrest believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, that the person whom he arrests is the person named in the warrant, he is protected from criminal responsibility in respect thereof to the same extent as if that person were the person named in the warrant.
@ref s 28(1) (src:739-740)
GIVEN `the person is authorized to execute a warrant to arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person believes, in good faith, that the person whom they arrest is the person named in the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person believes, on reasonable grounds, that the person whom they arrest is the person named in the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) the person is protected from criminal responsibility for arresting the person who is not the person named in the warrant` MEANS
    IF `the person is authorized to execute a warrant to arrest` AND `the person believes, in good faith, that the person whom they arrest is the person named in the warrant` AND `the person believes, on reasonable grounds, that the person whom they arrest is the person named in the warrant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person who is authorized to execute a warrant to arrest believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, that the person whom he arrests is the person named in the warrant"

-- src:741 | Person assisting
-- src:742 | (2) Where a person is authorized to execute a warrant to arrest,
-- src:743 | (a) every one who, being called on to assist him, believes that the person in whose arrest he is called on to assist is the person named in the warrant, and
-- src:744 | (b) every keeper of a prison who is required to receive and detain a person who he believes has been arrested under the warrant,
-- src:745 | is protected from criminal responsibility in respect thereof to the same extent as if that person were the person named in the warrant.
@ref s 28(2) (src:741-745)
DECLARE `s 28(2) the person` IS ONE OF
    `s 28(2)(a) a person who, being called on to assist the person authorized to execute the warrant, is called on to assist in an arrest`
    `s 28(2)(b) a keeper of a prison who is required to receive and detain a person`
    `s 28(2) another person`

@ref s 28(2) (src:741-745)
GIVEN `a person is authorized to execute a warrant to arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
      who IS A `s 28(2) the person`
      `the person believes that the person in whose arrest they are called on to assist is the person named in the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the keeper believes that the person they are required to receive and detain has been arrested under the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(2) the person is protected from criminal responsibility to the same extent as if the person arrested were the person named in the warrant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a person is authorized to execute a warrant to arrest` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is authorized to execute a warrant to arrest"
        IF who EQUALS `s 28(2)(a) a person who, being called on to assist the person authorized to execute the warrant, is called on to assist in an arrest` AND `the person believes that the person in whose arrest they are called on to assist is the person named in the warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF who EQUALS `s 28(2)(b) a keeper of a prison who is required to receive and detain a person` AND `the keeper believes that the person they are required to receive and detain has been arrested under the warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who, being called on to assist him, believes that the person in whose arrest he is called on to assist is the person named in the warrant" and "every keeper of a prison who is required to receive and detain a person who he believes has been arrested under the warrant"

§ `Section 29 -- Duty of person arresting`

-- src:746 | Duty of person arresting
-- src:747 | 29 (1) It is the duty of every one who executes a process or warrant to have it with him, where it is feasible to do so, and to produce it when requested to do so.
@ref s 29(1) (src:746-747)
DECLARE `s 29 the person who bears the duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 29 a person who executes a process or warrant`
    `s 29 a person who arrests a person, whether with or without a warrant`

DECLARE `s 29 the act the duty is to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 29(1) have the process or warrant with them`
    `s 29(1) produce the process or warrant when requested`
    `s 29(2) give notice of the process or warrant under which the arrest is made, or of the reason for the arrest`

@ref s 29(1) (src:746-747)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 29 the person who bears the duty` `s 29 the act the duty is to do`
`s 29(1) the duty to have the process or warrant with the person` MEANS
    PARTY `s 29 a person who executes a process or warrant`
    MUST `s 29(1) have the process or warrant with them`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person who executed the process or warrant did not have it with them, where it was feasible to do so"

@ref s 29(1) (src:746-747)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 29 the person who bears the duty` `s 29 the act the duty is to do`
`s 29(1) the duty to produce the process or warrant when requested` MEANS
    PARTY `s 29 a person who executes a process or warrant`
    MUST `s 29(1) produce the process or warrant when requested`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person who executed the process or warrant did not produce it when requested to do so"

@ref s 29(1) (src:746-747)
GIVEN `the person executes a process or warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is feasible to have it with them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(1) the person who executes a process or warrant has the duty to have it with them` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person executes a process or warrant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who executes a process or warrant"
        IF `it is feasible to have it with them` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to have it with him, where it is feasible to do so"

@ref s 29(1) (src:746-747)
GIVEN `the person executes a process or warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been requested to produce it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(1) the person who executes a process or warrant has the duty to produce it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person executes a process or warrant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who executes a process or warrant"
        IF `the person has been requested to produce it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to produce it when requested to do so"

-- src:748 | Notice
-- src:749 | (2) It is the duty of every one who arrests a person, whether with or without a warrant, to give notice to that person, where it is feasible to do so, of
-- src:750 | (a) the process or warrant under which he makes the arrest; or
-- src:751 | (b) the reason for the arrest.
@ref s 29(2) (src:748-751)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 29 the person who bears the duty` `s 29 the act the duty is to do`
`s 29(2) the duty to give notice of the process or warrant or of the reason for the arrest` MEANS
    PARTY `s 29 a person who arrests a person, whether with or without a warrant`
    MUST `s 29(2) give notice of the process or warrant under which the arrest is made, or of the reason for the arrest`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person who arrested did not give notice of the process or warrant under which the arrest was made, or of the reason for the arrest, where it was feasible to do so"

@ref s 29(2) (src:748-751)
GIVEN `the person arrests a person, whether with or without a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is feasible to give notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(2) the person who arrests has the duty to give the person arrested notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person arrests a person, whether with or without a warrant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who arrests a person, whether with or without a warrant"
        IF `it is feasible to give notice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to give notice to that person, where it is feasible to do so"

@ref s 29(2) (src:750-751)
DECLARE `s 29(2) the notice is of` IS ONE OF
    `s 29(2)(a) the process or warrant under which the arrest is made`
    `s 29(2)(b) the reason for the arrest`
    `s 29(2) neither`

@ref s 29(2) (src:750-751)
GIVEN notice IS A `s 29(2) the notice is of`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(2) the notice discharges the duty` MEANS
    IF notice EQUALS `s 29(2) neither`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two kinds of notice and does not say what a notice of neither is worth
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:752 | Failure to comply
-- src:753 | (3) Failure to comply with subsection (1) or (2) does not of itself deprive a person who executes a process or warrant, or a person who makes an arrest, or those who assist them, of protection from criminal responsibility.
@ref s 29(3) (src:752-753)
GIVEN `the person failed to comply with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that failure is the only ground said to deprive the person of protection from criminal responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(3) the failure deprives the person of protection from criminal responsibility` MEANS
    IF `the person failed to comply with subsection (1) or (2)` AND `that failure is the only ground said to deprive the person of protection from criminal responsibility`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with subsection (1) or (2) does not of itself deprive a person who executes a process or warrant, or a person who makes an arrest, or those who assist them, of protection from criminal responsibility."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "of itself": the subsection says nothing of a failure together with other grounds

§ `Sections 30 and 31 -- Preventing and arresting for a breach of the peace`

-- src:754 | Preventing breach of peace
-- src:755 | 30 Every one who witnesses a breach of the peace is justified in interfering to prevent the continuance or renewal thereof and may detain any person who commits or is about to join in or to renew the breach of the peace, for the purpose of giving him into the custody of a peace officer, if he uses no more force than is reasonably necessary to prevent the continuance or renewal of the breach of the peace or than is reasonably proportioned to the danger to be apprehended from the continuance or renewal of the breach of the peace.
@ref s 30 (src:754-755)
GIVEN `the person witnesses a breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interference is to prevent the continuance or renewal of the breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30 the person is justified in interfering to prevent the continuance or renewal of the breach of the peace` MEANS
    IF `the person witnesses a breach of the peace` AND `the interference is to prevent the continuance or renewal of the breach of the peace`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who witnesses a breach of the peace is justified in interfering to prevent the continuance or renewal thereof"

@ref s 30 (src:755-755)
GIVEN `the person witnesses a breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person detained commits, is about to join in or is about to renew the breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is giving the person detained into the custody of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no more force is used than is reasonably necessary to prevent the continuance or renewal of the breach of the peace or than is reasonably proportioned to the danger to be apprehended from the continuance or renewal of the breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30 the person may detain the person who commits or is about to join in or to renew the breach of the peace` MEANS
    IF `the person witnesses a breach of the peace` AND `the person detained commits, is about to join in or is about to renew the breach of the peace` AND `the purpose is giving the person detained into the custody of a peace officer`
       AND `no more force is used than is reasonably necessary to prevent the continuance or renewal of the breach of the peace or than is reasonably proportioned to the danger to be apprehended from the continuance or renewal of the breach of the peace`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may detain any person who commits or is about to join in or to renew the breach of the peace, for the purpose of giving him into the custody of a peace officer, if he uses no more force than is reasonably necessary"

-- src:756 | Arrest for breach of peace
-- src:757 | 31 (1) Every peace officer who witnesses a breach of the peace and every one who lawfully assists the peace officer is justified in arresting any person whom he finds committing the breach of the peace or who, on reasonable grounds, he believes is about to join in or renew the breach of the peace.
-- src:758 | Giving person in charge
-- src:759 | (2) Every peace officer is justified in receiving into custody any person who is given into his charge as having been a party to a breach of the peace by one who has, or who on reasonable grounds the peace officer believes has, witnessed the breach of the peace.
@ref s 31(1) (src:756-759)
DECLARE `s 31(1) the person is` IS ONE OF
    `s 31(1) a peace officer who witnesses a breach of the peace`
    `s 31(1) a person who lawfully assists the peace officer`
    `s 31(1) another person`

@ref s 31(1) (src:756-757)
GIVEN who IS A `s 31(1) the person is`
      `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person arrested is found committing the breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person on reasonable grounds believes that the person arrested is about to join in or renew the breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) the person is justified in arresting the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF who EQUALS `s 31(1) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every peace officer who witnesses a breach of the peace and every one who lawfully assists the peace officer"
        IF who EQUALS `s 31(1) a peace officer who witnesses a breach of the peace` AND `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a peace officer is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF who EQUALS `s 31(1) a peace officer who witnesses a breach of the peace` AND `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every peace officer who witnesses a breach of the peace"
        IF `the person arrested is found committing the breach of the peace` OR `the person on reasonable grounds believes that the person arrested is about to join in or renew the breach of the peace` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person whom he finds committing the breach of the peace or who, on reasonable grounds, he believes is about to join in or renew the breach of the peace"

-- src:758 | Giving person in charge
-- src:759 | (2) Every peace officer is justified in receiving into custody any person who is given into his charge as having been a party to a breach of the peace by one who has, or who on reasonable grounds the peace officer believes has, witnessed the breach of the peace.
@ref s 31(2) (src:758-759)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is given into the peace officer's charge as having been a party to a breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who gives them into charge has witnessed the breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer on reasonable grounds believes that the person who gives them into charge has witnessed the breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2) the peace officer is justified in receiving the person into custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a peace officer is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every peace officer is justified in receiving into custody"
        IF `the person is given into the peace officer's charge as having been a party to a breach of the peace` AND (`the person who gives them into charge has witnessed the breach of the peace` OR `the peace officer on reasonable grounds believes that the person who gives them into charge has witnessed the breach of the peace`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who is given into his charge as having been a party to a breach of the peace by one who has, or who on reasonable grounds the peace officer believes has, witnessed the breach of the peace"

§ `Sections 32 and 33 -- Suppression of riots`

-- src:761 | Suppression of Riots
-- src:762 | Use of force to suppress riot
-- src:763 | 32 (1) Every peace officer is justified in using or in ordering the use of as much force as the peace officer believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds,
-- src:764 | (a) is necessary to suppress a riot; and
-- src:765 | (b) is not excessive, having regard to the danger to be apprehended from the continuance of the riot.
@ref s 32(1) (src:761-765)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, that the force is necessary to suppress a riot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, that the force is not excessive, having regard to the danger to be apprehended from the continuance of the riot` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) the peace officer is justified in using or in ordering the use of the force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a peace officer is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every peace officer is justified in using or in ordering the use of"
        IF `the peace officer believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, that the force is necessary to suppress a riot` AND `the peace officer believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, that the force is not excessive, having regard to the danger to be apprehended from the continuance of the riot` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as much force as the peace officer believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds"

-- src:766 | Person bound by military law
-- src:767 | (2) Every one who is bound by military law to obey the command of his superior officer is justified in obeying any command given by his superior officer for the suppression of a riot unless the order is manifestly unlawful.
@ref s 32(2) (src:766-767)
GIVEN `the person is bound by military law to obey the command of their superior officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the command is given by their superior officer for the suppression of a riot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is manifestly unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the person is justified in obeying the command` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is bound by military law to obey the command of their superior officer` AND `the command is given by their superior officer for the suppression of a riot`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who is bound by military law to obey the command of his superior officer is justified in obeying any command given by his superior officer for the suppression of a riot"
        IF `the order is manifestly unlawful` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the order is manifestly unlawful"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:768 | Obeying order of peace officer
-- src:769 | (3) Every one is justified in obeying an order of a peace officer to use force to suppress a riot if
-- src:770 | (a) he acts in good faith; and
-- src:771 | (b) the order is not manifestly unlawful.
@ref s 32(3) (src:768-771)
GIVEN `the order is an order of a peace officer to use force to suppress a riot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is not manifestly unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(3) the person is justified in obeying the order of a peace officer to use force to suppress a riot` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order is an order of a peace officer to use force to suppress a riot` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "obeying an order of a peace officer to use force to suppress a riot"
        IF `the person acts in good faith` AND `the order is not manifestly unlawful` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is justified in obeying an order of a peace officer to use force to suppress a riot if (a) he acts in good faith; and (b) the order is not manifestly unlawful"

-- src:772 | Apprehension of serious mischief
-- src:773 | (4) Every one who, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, believes that serious mischief will result from a riot before it is possible to secure the attendance of a peace officer is justified in using as much force as he believes in good faith and on reasonable grounds,
-- src:774 | (a) is necessary to suppress the riot; and
-- src:775 | (b) is not excessive, having regard to the danger to be apprehended from the continuance of the riot.
@ref s 32(4) (src:772-775)
GIVEN `the person, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, believes that serious mischief will result from a riot before it is possible to secure the attendance of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, that the force is necessary to suppress the riot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, that the force is not excessive, having regard to the danger to be apprehended from the continuance of the riot` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(4) the person is justified in using the force` MEANS
    IF `the person, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, believes that serious mischief will result from a riot before it is possible to secure the attendance of a peace officer`
       AND `the person believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, that the force is necessary to suppress the riot`
       AND `the person believes, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, that the force is not excessive, having regard to the danger to be apprehended from the continuance of the riot`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who, in good faith and on reasonable grounds, believes that serious mischief will result from a riot before it is possible to secure the attendance of a peace officer is justified in using as much force as he believes in good faith and on reasonable grounds"

-- src:776 | Question of law
-- src:777 | (5) For the purposes of this section, the question whether an order is manifestly unlawful or not is a question of law.
@ref s 32(5) (src:776-777)
GIVEN `the question arises for the purposes of section 32 and is whether an order is manifestly unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(5) the question whether an order is manifestly unlawful is a question of law` MEANS
    IF `the question arises for the purposes of section 32 and is whether an order is manifestly unlawful`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of this section, the question whether an order is manifestly unlawful or not is a question of law"

-- src:778 | Duty of officers if rioters do not disperse
-- src:779 | 33 (1) Where the proclamation referred to in section 67 has been made or an offence against paragraph 68(a) or (b) has been committed, it is the duty of a peace officer and of a person who is lawfully required by him to assist, to disperse or to arrest persons who do not comply with the proclamation.
@ref s 33(1) (src:778-779)
DECLARE `s 33(1) the act the duty is to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 33(1) disperse or arrest persons who do not comply with the proclamation`

@ref s 33(1) (src:778-779)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 33(1) the act the duty is to do`
`s 33(1) the duty of the peace officer to disperse or arrest persons who do not comply with the proclamation` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `s 33(1) disperse or arrest persons who do not comply with the proclamation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the peace officer did not disperse or arrest persons who did not comply with the proclamation"

@ref s 33(1) (src:778-779)
GIVEN `the proclamation referred to in section 67 has been made, or an offence against paragraph 68(a) or (b) has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is lawfully required by a peace officer to assist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons do not comply with the proclamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(1) the person has the duty to disperse or to arrest persons who do not comply with the proclamation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proclamation referred to in section 67 has been made, or an offence against paragraph 68(a) or (b) has been committed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the proclamation referred to in section 67 has been made or an offence against paragraph 68(a) or (b) has been committed"
        IF `the person is a peace officer or lawfully required to assist` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a peace officer is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF `the person is a peace officer or lawfully required to assist` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is the duty of a peace officer and of a person who is lawfully required by him to assist"
        IF NOT `the persons do not comply with the proclamation` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "persons who do not comply with the proclamation"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the person is a peace officer or lawfully required to assist` MEANS `ccc1 either of` `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `the person is lawfully required by a peace officer to assist`)

-- src:780 | Protection of officers
-- src:781 | (2) No civil or criminal proceedings lie against a peace officer or a person who is lawfully required by a peace officer to assist him in respect of any death or injury that by reason of resistance is caused as a result of the performance by the peace officer or that person of a duty that is imposed by subsection (1).
@ref s 33(2) (src:780-781)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is lawfully required by a peace officer to assist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the death or injury is caused by reason of resistance as a result of the performance of a duty that is imposed by subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(2) civil or criminal proceedings lie against the person in respect of the death or injury` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a peace officer or lawfully required to assist` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a peace officer is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF `the person is a peace officer or lawfully required to assist` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against a peace officer or a person who is lawfully required by a peace officer to assist him"
        IF `the death or injury is caused by reason of resistance as a result of the performance of a duty that is imposed by subsection (1)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No civil or criminal proceedings lie against a peace officer or a person who is lawfully required by a peace officer to assist him"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of any death or injury that by reason of resistance is caused as a result of the performance by the peace officer or that person of a duty that is imposed by subsection (1)"
    WHERE
        `the person is a peace officer or lawfully required to assist` MEANS `ccc1 either of` `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `the person is lawfully required by a peace officer to assist`)

-- src:782 | Section not restrictive
-- src:783 | (3) Nothing in this section limits or affects any powers, duties or functions that are conferred or imposed by this Act with respect to the suppression of riots.
@ref s 33(3) (src:782-783)
GIVEN `the power, duty or function is conferred or imposed by this Act with respect to the suppression of riots` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(3) section 33 limits or affects the power, duty or function` MEANS
    IF `the power, duty or function is conferred or imposed by this Act with respect to the suppression of riots`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section limits or affects any powers, duties or functions that are conferred or imposed by this Act with respect to the suppression of riots."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any powers, duties or functions that are conferred or imposed by this Act with respect to the suppression of riots"
